<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.2.2: Constant and Exponential Change</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01758</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.2.2: Constant and Exponential Change</md:title>
    <md:uuid>618817ff-e0ac-4023-8e4b-641bec86f60d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Pattern 1</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Pattern. Step 0,1 dot. Step 1, 3 dots, 2 by 2 with upper left dot removed. Step 2, 5 dots, 3 by 2 with upper left dot removed. Step 3, 7 dots, 4 by 2 with upper left dot removed.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_04_03_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
      </para>
      <para>Pattern 2</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Pattern. Step 0, 0 dots. Step 1, 1 dot. Step 2, 4 dots, arranged 2 by 2. Step 3, 9 dots, arranged 3 by 3.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_04_03_02.svg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
      </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Look at Pattern 1.</para>
          <para> How is the number of dots in each step changing?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Each step has 2 rows of dots, with each row having the same number of dots as the step number, plus one extra
      dot.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> How many dots will be in Step 5 in the pattern, and how will they be arranged?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>In Step 5, there will be 2 rows of 5 dots plus one additional dot.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Look at Pattern 2.</para>
          <para> How is the number of dots in each step changing?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Each step has as many rows and columns of dots as the step number.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> How many dots will be in Step 5 in the pattern, and how will they be arranged?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Step 5 is a 5-by-5 array of dots.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <para>Consider the following table.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-wideadjustedtable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
        Step
      </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
        Number of dots in Pattern 1
      </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
        Number of dots in Pattern 2
      </emphasis>
            </entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>
        0
      </entry>
            <entry>
        1
      </entry>
            <entry>
        0
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
        1
      </entry>
            <entry>
        3
      </entry>
            <entry>
        1
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
        2
      </entry>
            <entry>
        5
      </entry>
            <entry>
        4
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
        3
      </entry>
            <entry>
        7
      </entry>
            <entry>
        9
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
        4
      </entry>
            <entry/>
            <entry/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
        5
      </entry>
            <entry/>
            <entry/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
        10
      </entry>
            <entry/>
            <entry/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
        12
      </entry>
            <entry/>
            <entry/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
        \(n\)
      </entry>
            <entry/>
            <entry/>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
        <item>Complete the table with the number of dots for Pattern 1.</item>
      </list>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Activity</title>
        <exercise id="8095bb6a-6ede-482f-978e-394579c2a588" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> In Step 4, what is the number of dots in Pattern 1?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Step 4 has 9 dots in Pattern 1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 9. Step 4 has 9 dots in Pattern 1. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="8139dd15-22b1-4be7-9a65-6a4492b88b72" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> In Step 5, what is the number of dots in Pattern 1?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Step 5 has 11 dots in Pattern 1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 11. Step 5 has 11 dots in Pattern 1.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="9330201a-1aa8-48b6-b4c5-f7beef96cfe7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> In Step 10, what is the number of dots in Pattern 1?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Step 10 has 21 dots in Pattern 1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 21. Step 10 has 21 dots in Pattern 1.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a74ee2de-72ef-4d03-bd65-da607a8f852e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> In Step 12, what is the number of dots in Pattern 1?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Step 12 has 25 dots in Pattern 1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 25. Step 12 has 25 dots in Pattern 1.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> In Step \(n\), what is the number of dots in Pattern 1?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(2n+1\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
        <item>Complete the table with the number of dots for Pattern 2.</item>
      </list>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="2b787d9d-44ad-4bb3-a433-1acdd39ddf49" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> In Step 4, what is the number of dots in Pattern 2?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Step 4 has 16 dots in Pattern 2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 16. Step 4 has 16 dots in Pattern 2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="277c86eb-6bf2-4c19-824e-49ea954daf66" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> In Step 5, what is the number of dots in Pattern 2?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Step 5 has 25 dots in Pattern 2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 25. Step 5 has 25 dots in Pattern 2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="95eaf6ac-0fbb-4732-9a7e-d258e1c80258" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> In Step 10, what is the number of dots in Pattern 2?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Step 10 has 100 dots in Pattern 2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 100. Step 10 has 100 dots in Pattern 2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="af51617b-17bb-4e0d-9cd3-c26d38266205" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> In Step 12, what is the number of dots in Pattern 2?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Step 12 has 144 dots in Pattern 2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 144. Step 12 has 144 dots in Pattern 2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> In Step \(n\), what is the number of dots in Pattern 2?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(n \cdot n\) or \(n^2\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
        <item>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Plot the number of dots at each step number for Pattern 1
    and Pattern 2.</item>
      </list>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para> Pattern 1 </para>
            <para>Select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="Points plotted on a grid. Number of dots. Step number.">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_04_03_03.svg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
            </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para> Pattern 2 </para>
            <para>Select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="Points plotted on a grid. Number of dots. Step number.">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_04_03_04.svg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
            </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Explain why the graphs of the two patterns look the way they do.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>The points representing the first pattern lie on a line because getting from one step to the next involves adding
      the same number of dots (2 dots). The points representing the second pattern do not lie on a line. They
      “curve” upward because the number of dots added at each step increases from step to step.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
